      }
     ]
    ],
    [
     [
      {
       "t": "code",
       "v": "schema"
      }
     ],
     [
      "where the extension's JSON Schema for this version is published — an immutable URL"
     ]
    ],
    [
     [
      {
       "t": "code",
       "v": "requires"
      }
     ],
     [
      "the extensions it depends on, each with a version range (Core ",
      {
       "t": "a",
       "href": "/floorspec/core/extensions#12.3",
       "c": [
        "12.3"
       ]
      },
      "); never a cycle"
     ]
    ],
    [
     [
      {
       "t": "code",
       "v": "kinds"
      }
     ],
     [
      "the kinds of element it adds, each named by the collection that holds them in a document (Core ",
      {
       "t": "a",
       "href": "/floorspec/core/extensions#12.5",
       "c": [
        "12.5"
       ]
      },
      "), and which optional parts of a fallback — a glTF ",
      {
       "t": "code",
       "v": "asset"
      },
      ", a 2D ",
      {
       "t": "code",
       "v": "symbol"
      },
      " — every element of the kind must carry"
     ]
    ],
    [
     [
      {
       "t": "code",
       "v": "terms"
      }
     ],
     [
      "the room-function terms it adds (Core ",
      {
       "t": "a",
       "href": "/floorspec/core/taxonomy#4.2",
       "c": [
        "4.2"
       ]
      },
      "), without the ",
      {
       "t": "code",
       "v": "<NAME>:"
      },
      " prefix"
     ]
    ],
    [
     [
      {
       "t": "code",
       "v": "implementations"
      }
     ],
     [
      "software that implements it, by name and URL"
     ]
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "c": [
    "A validator configured with these entries as its ",
    {
     "t": "strong",
     "c": [
      "known extensions"
     ]
    },
    " checks that a document using an extension at a known version also uses what it requires, at versions in range, and uses only the collections and terms the entry names (Core ",
    {
     "t": "a",
     "href": "/floorspec/core/extensions#12.3",
     "c": [
      "12.3"
     ]
    },
    ", ",
    {
     "t": "a",
     "href": "/floorspec/core/extensions#12.4",
     "c": [
      "12.4"
     ]
    },
    "). A validator never needs the registry to read a document: known extensions only add checks."
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "h",
   "depth": 2,
   "id": "lifecycle",
   "c": [
    "Lifecycle"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "c": [
    "An extension moves through four statuses, each a value of the entry's ",
    {
     "t": "code",
     "v": "status"
    },
    ", and every move is a pull request to this repository (FLR-REQ-138) made with the extension template (",
    {
     "t": "a",
     "href": "https://github.com/matdemers1/floorspec/tree/8a99d02b3a2111aacd9ed81c3e415af47f73505e/.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE/extension.md",
     "c": [
      {
       "t": "code",
       "v": ".github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE/extension.md"
      }
     ]
    },
    ": add ",
    {
     "t": "code",
     "v": "?template=extension.md"
    },
    " to the pull request's URL). The Registry workflow (",
    {
     "t": "code",
     "v": ".github/workflows/registry.yml"
    },
    ") runs ",
    {
     "t": "a",
     "href": "https://github.com/matdemers1/floorspec/tree/8a99d02b3a2111aacd9ed81c3e415af47f73505e/tools/registry-gates.ts",
     "c": [
      {
       "t": "code",
       "v": "tools/registry-gates.ts"
      }
     ]
    },
    " — ",
    {
     "t": "code",
     "v": "pnpm registry:check"
    },
    " — on every push and pull request, and fails when an entry does not have what its status asks or a change is not a step the lifecycle allows. Each status keeps the requirements of the one before it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "table",
   "align": [
    null,
    null,
    null
   ],
   "head": [
    [
     "Status"
    ],
    [
     "What it means"
    ],
    [
     "What the gates require"
    ]
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     [
      {
       "t": "strong",
       "c": [
        "Proposal"
       ]
      },
      " (",
      {
       "t": "code",
       "v": "proposal"
      },
      ")"
     ],
     [
      "an idea, with its name reserved"
     ],
     [
      {
       "t": "code",
       "v": "extension.json"
      },
      " matching the entry schema, in a directory named after it; ",
      {
       "t": "code",
       "v": "proposal.md"
      },
      ", the written rationale — what it describes, why it is not Core or an existing extension, who means to implement it; a row in a table below"
     ]
    ],
    [
     [
      {
       "t": "strong",
       "c": [
        "Draft"
       ]
      },
      " (",
      {
       "t": "code",
       "v": "draft"
      },
      ")"
     ],
     [
      "specified, and changing"
     ],
     [
      {
       "t": "code",
       "v": "spec.md"
      },
      " with its statements tagged in an ID space of its own, its 1.1 table giving the entry's version and status; a schema file whose ",
      {
       "t": "code",
       "v": "$id"
      },
      " is the entry's ",
      {
       "t": "code",
       "v": "schema"
      },
      ", a URL with a ",
      {
       "t": "code",
       "v": "/<version>/"
      },
      " segment; a conformance suite at ",
      {
       "t": "code",
       "v": "conformance/ext/<NAME>/<version>/"
      },
      " with a test for every ",
      {
       "t": "code",
       "v": "MUST"
      },
      " and ",
      {
       "t": "code",
       "v": "MUST NOT"
      }
     ]
    ],
    [
     [
      {
       "t": "strong",
       "c": [
        "Release Candidate"
       ]
      },
      " (",
      {
       "t": "code",
       "v": "releaseCandidate"
      },
      ")"
     ],
     [
      "specified and frozen, unless implementations find a problem"
     ],
     [
      "at least one implementation in ",
      {
       "t": "code",
       "v": "implementations"
      },
      ", each with ",
      {
       "t": "strong",
       "c": [
        "evidence"
       ]
      },
      " that it passed every test of the suite — or an owner's recorded ",
      {
       "t": "strong",
       "c": [
        "exception"
       ]
      }
     ]
    ],
    [
     [
      {
       "t": "strong",
       "c": [
        "Ratified"
       ]
      },
      " (",
      {
       "t": "code",
       "v": "ratified"
      },
      ")"
     ],
     [
      "stable"
     ],
     [
      "at least two implementations, each with evidence of passing the suite as it is now, two of them ",
      {
       "t": "strong",
       "c": [
        "independent"
       ]
      },
      " (FLR-REQ-092; the entry schema itself refuses a ratified entry with fewer than two); from the commit that ratifies it, its schema files, its suite and every member of its entry but ",
      {
       "t": "code",
       "v": "implementations"
      },
      " are frozen"
     ]
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "c": [
    {
     "t": "strong",
     "c": [
      "The oracle is not evidence."
     ]
    },
    " The conformance oracle (",
    {
     "t": "code",
     "v": "tools/oracle/ext/"
    },
    ") implements every official extension, but it wrote the expected outputs its suite is checked against, so its passing proves nothing about the suite. An implementation is software that someone uses: D3 Floorspec's engine is one, and is listed for every official extension."
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "h",
   "depth": 3,
   "id": "changes-by-pull-request",
   "c": [
    "Changes by pull request"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "c": [
    "On a pull request the gates also compare each entry with the pull request's base:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "p",
      "c": [
       "a new extension, and a new version of an existing one, enters as a Proposal or a Draft;"
      ]
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "t": "p",
      "c": [
       "a version moves forward one status per pull request, and never back — a problem found in a Release Candidate or a Ratified version is fixed in a new version;"
      ]
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "t": "p",
      "c": [
       "a version only ever increases, and an entry is never removed: its name stays reserved, and its earlier versions stay recoverable from this repository's history and at their published URLs."
      ]
     }
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "c": [
    "A maintainer may allow anything else — two steps at once, a withdrawn proposal — by adding the ",
    {
     "t": "code",
     "v": "registry-maintainer"
    },
    " label to the pull request, which re-runs the gates, and says why in it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "h",
   "depth": 3,
   "id": "evidence",
   "c": [
    "Evidence"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "c": [
    "Evidence that an implementation passes a version's suite is a file ",
    {
     "t": "code",
     "v": "registry/<NAME>/evidence/<slug>.json"
    },
    ", one for each implementation listed:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "code",
   "lang": "json",
   "v": "{\n  \"implementation\": { \"name\": \"D3 Floorspec (@floorspec/engine)\", \"url\": \"https://github.com/matdemers1/d3-floorspec\", \"version\": \"ee6939f64cbfbf92f0ade7112cbe8df62744853a\" },\n  \"maintainer\": \"matdemers1\",\n  \"sharesCodeWith\": [],\n  \"extension\": \"FS_plumbing\",\n  \"extensionVersion\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"suite\": { \"commit\": \"441a066de5285ce7998e045e1add1bffa92d58a0\", \"tests\": 39 },\n  \"result\": { \"passed\": 39, \"failed\": 0 },\n  \"ran\": \"2026-10-05\",\n  \"run\": \"https://github.com/matdemers1/d3-floorspec/actions/runs/37276088906\",\n  \"command\": \"pnpm --filter @floorspec/engine conformance (test/extensions.node.test.ts)\"\n}"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "c": [
    {
     "t": "code",
     "v": "implementation"
    },
    " is the entry's listing — the same ",
    {
     "t": "code",
     "v": "name"
    },
    " and ",
    {
     "t": "code",
     "v": "url"
    },
    " — with the version that ran; ",
    {
     "t": "code",
     "v": "suite.commit"
    },
    " is the commit of this repository whose ",
    {
     "t": "code",
     "v": "conformance/ext/<NAME>/<version>/"
    },
    " it ran, and ",
    {
     "t": "code",
     "v": "suite.tests"
    },
    " how many tests that suite held then, which the gates check against the commit; ",
    {
     "t": "code",
     "v": "result"
    },
    " must be every test passed and none failed. ",
    {
     "t": "code",
     "v": "run"
    },
    " links a public run — a CI job — and ",
    {
     "t": "code",
     "v": "ran"
    },
    " is its date. Evidence of a suite that has changed since its commit is ",
    {
     "t": "strong",
     "c": [
      "stale"
     ]
    },
    ": a warning for a Release Candidate, which means the implementation should run the suite again, and an error for a Ratified version."
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "c": [
    "Two implementations are ",
    {
     "t": "strong",
     "c": [
      "independent"
     ]
    },
    " when their evidence names different ",
    {
     "t": "code",
     "v": "maintainer"
    },
    "s and neither lists the other in ",
    {
     "t": "code",
     "v": "sharesCodeWith"
    },
    " — the implementations it shares code with, a parser, a geometry kernel, a port. The pull request that ratifies says how they came to be written independently; the maintainers judge it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "h",
   "depth": 3,
   "id": "exceptions",
   "c": [
    "Exceptions"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "c": [
    "An owner may waive one gate for one version of one extension, by an entry in ",
    {
     "t": "a",
     "href": "https://github.com/matdemers1/floorspec/tree/8a99d02b3a2111aacd9ed81c3e415af47f73505e/registry/exceptions.json",
     "c": [
      {
       "t": "code",
       "v": "exceptions.json"
      }
     ]
    },
    " that names the decision and the condition that ends it. Only the Release Candidate's implementation rule can be waived (",
    {
     "t": "code",
     "v": "releaseCandidate.implementation"
    },
    "); nothing of Ratified can. The gates fail when an exception names an entry or version that is not there, or a rule that now passes, so an exception is removed when it ends. There are none: the last, FS_furniture 0.1.0's, published as a Release Candidate with no implementation (FLR-T-8.3), ended when D3 Floorspec's engine passed its suite and was listed."
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "h",
   "depth": 3,
   "id": "who-decides",
   "c": [
    "Who decides"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "c": [
    "The registry's maintainers — the owners of ",
    {
     "t": "code",
     "v": "registry/"
    },
    " in ",
    {
     "t": "a",
     "href": "https://github.com/matdemers1/floorspec/tree/8a99d02b3a2111aacd9ed81c3e415af47f73505e/.github/CODEOWNERS",
     "c": [
      {
       "t": "code",
       "v": ".github/CODEOWNERS"
      }
     ]
    },
    " — review every registry pull request, judge what the gates cannot (that a proposal belongs in the registry, that a specification is clear, that two implementations are independent, that a Release Candidate is ready to freeze), add the ",
    {
     "t": "code",
     "v": "registry-maintainer"
    },
    " label, and record exceptions. The gates decide nothing a maintainer could not see; they make sure nothing is merged that the lifecycle forbids."
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "c": [
    "Every kind an extension adds carries a fallback — a box, and optionally a glTF model and a 2D symbol — so that a reader without the extension still shows that something is there. An extension never changes what core data means (Core ",
    {
     "t": "a",
     "href": "/floorspec/core/extensions#12.7",
     "c": [
      "12.7"
     ]
    },
    "). Building systems — electrical, plumbing, mechanical, low-voltage, structural, furniture — ship as first-party ",
    {
     "t": "code",
     "v": "FS_"
    },
    " extensions (FLR-ADR-001)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "h",
   "depth": 2,
   "id": "official-extensions",
   "c": [
    "Official extensions"
   ]
  },
